  "mechanism_of_action": {
    "plain_language": "FT536 is an engineered natural killer (NK) cell therapy derived from induced pluripotent stem cells (iPSCs) designed to target and eliminate cancer cells expressing MICA/B antigens. It is modified to express a chimeric antigen receptor (CAR) targeting MICA/B, CD16 for enhanced antibody-dependent cellular cytotoxicity, and IL-15RF for improved persistence and activity. CD38 is eliminated to prevent fratricide and enhance efficacy.",
